# Orientation Day Pamphlet Corrections

**Author:** Aisha Kabir  
**Date:** March 26, 2026  
**Purpose:** To provide corrected pages for the orientation day pamphlets after a minor error was discovered in the original print.

---

## Summary of Corrections

Following a review of the orientation day pamphlets, a minor error was identified in the event schedule section. This required immediate adjustments and reprinting of specific pages to ensure the accuracy of the information provided to attendees. Below are the corrected details.

---

## Corrected Sections

### 1. Event Schedule (Page 3)

**Original Issue:**
- The start time of the Dean of Engineering's opening lecture was incorrectly listed as **9:30 AM** instead of the correct time, **10:00 AM**.
- The location for the breakout sessions was missing room assignments for the STEM majors.

**Updated Details:**

#### Orientation Day Schedule
| Time       | Event                                      | Location             |
|------------|-------------------------------------------|----------------------|
| **8:30 AM** | Registration and Welcome Breakfast         | Main Hall, Lobby     |
| **10:00 AM** | Opening Lecture by Dean of Engineering    | Auditorium, Room A1  |
| **11:00 AM** | Breakout Sessions                         | Various Locations    |
|            | - STEM Majors: Room B2                    |                      |
|            | - Humanities Majors: Room B3              |                      |
|            | - Business Majors: Room B4                |                      |
| **12:30 PM** | Networking Lunch                         | Outdoor Courtyard    |
| **2:00 PM**  | Campus Tours                             | Meet at Main Hall    |

---

### 2. Welcome Message (Page 1)

**Original Issue:**
- A typographical error was present in the Dean of Engineering's title, which was incorrectly written as "Dean of Engeering."

**Updated Text:**
> Welcome to Orientation Day 2026!  
> We are thrilled to have you join our vibrant academic community. This pamphlet contains all the essential information you need to make the most of your first day on campus.  
> **Keynote Speaker:** Dr. Jonathan Reeves, Dean of Engineering  
> We look forward to an exciting year ahead filled with learning, growth, and success!

---

### 3. Contact Information (Page 6)

**Original Issue:**
- The email address for the admissions office was outdated and no longer in use.

**Updated Details:**

#### Contact Information
- **Admissions Office:** admissions@university.edu  
- **Event Logistics Team:** logistics@university.edu  
- **Technical Support:** techsupport@university.edu  
- **Campus Tours Coordinator:** tours@university.edu  

---

## Actions Taken

1. **Reprinting Process:**
   - Corrected pages were reprinted and verified by the communications team.
   - A total of 500 corrected pamphlets were produced to replace the original batch.

2. **Quality Assurance:**
   - Each pamphlet underwent a final review to confirm the accuracy of the updated information.
   - Staff members were briefed on the changes to ensure consistent communication with attendees.

3. **Distribution Plan:**
   - Corrected pamphlets will be distributed on orientation day at the registration desk.
   - An email with the updated schedule will also be sent to all registered attendees.

---

## Additional Notes

- The logistics team has confirmed that all audiovisual equipment requested by the Dean of Engineering for his opening lecture will be available and operational by 9:00 AM on the day of the event.
- Staff members assigned to breakout sessions have been notified of their updated room assignments.
- The online orientation portal has been updated with the corrected schedule to reflect the changes.

---

## Approval and Acknowledgments

This document was prepared by **Aisha Kabir** from the communications team and approved by the orientation planning committee. Special thanks to the logistics and IT teams for their swift action in resolving issues to ensure a seamless orientation experience.

